{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nSplit out of 06e0-fb68-657a-4ea1 (effete-barbaric-xiaosaurus). `reducer` is ONE\nun-annotated def away from the tier-1 typing ratchet — but that one def is not a\nrubber-stamp annotation, which is why it was excluded rather than papered over.\n\n## The problem\n`rebar.reducer._filters.match_predicate(state, field, op, value)` takes `value` whose\ntype DEPENDS ON `op`: a scalar for `eq`/`lt`/`le`/`gt`/`ge`, an iterable for `in`, and a\n`(lo, hi)` pair for `range`. Annotating it `value: object` was tried and produces 7 real\nmypy errors in the body (`object` is not iterable, no `int()` overload, etc.).\n`value: Any` would satisfy the ratchet while buying neither the navigability nor the\ncontract driver — exactly the failure mode ticket cc77-8120-bcc6-47e8 documents.\n\n## Approach\nModel the predicate properly rather than widening: an operator-tagged `PredicateValue`\nunion defined in `_filters.py` (a `str` scalar for `eq`/`lt`/`le`/`gt`/`ge`, an\n`AbstractSet[str]` for `in`, and a `tuple[str | None, str | None]` pair for `range`), so\nthe operator and its value shape travel together and the body narrows by construction\n(isinstance narrowing inside per-field helpers extracted along the existing\ntag/priority/string-field seams — which also brings `match_predicate`'s baselined\nC901=17 DOWN, never up). The value has three in-package consumers/producers, all\ncovered:\n\n1. `reducer/_query.py` — `_parse_value` PRODUCES the value; tighten its return to\n   `tuple[str, PredicateValue]` so the parser builds exactly the shape the matcher\n   consumes.\n2. `reducer/_filters.py::apply_ticket_filters` — builds `set[str]` values for `in` and a\n   scalar for `eq`; already conforms, now checked against the annotation.\n3. `reducer/search.py::search_states` (line ~206) — the pass-through: unpacks\n   `(f, op, val, neg)` tuples from `parse_query` (and its `parent_resolver` rewrite maps\n   an `eq` str value to another str, shape-preserving) and forwards `val` to\n   `match_predicate`. The forwarded value stays inside the `PredicateValue` union by\n   construction; the module is re-verified under\n   `mypy src/rebar/reducer --disallow-untyped-defs` like the rest of the package, and no\n   signature change is expected there (the existing `match_predicate(state, field, op,\n   value)` call shape is preserved, so `search.py` and the unit tests keep passing\n   unmodified).\n\nThen promote `rebar.reducer.*` into the tier-1 override in pyproject.toml and\n`_RATCHET_BASELINE` in tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mypy src/rebar/reducer --disallow-untyped-defs` is clean with NO new `: Any`/`-> Any`.\n- [ ] `rebar.reducer.*` is in the tier-1 override and pinned in `_RATCHET_BASELINE`.\n- [ ] Filter/query behaviour is unchanged (existing reducer filter tests pass unmodified)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787374190124318001,"uuid":"030338e6-a323-4cf9-9e9d-56f57ddef488"}